The oblique design holds up across layers and phrasings on held-out facts: guess attention falls to ≤0.05 nearly everywhere (for example L10.H2 in phrasings A/B/D: 0.45 with original weights, 0.39 with the current edit, 0.02 with the oblique one), question attention rises towards no-guess levels (L10.H0/H2 0.82/0.95 on dev TEST; L12 0.35–0.54), and no-guess attention changes less than with the current edits (L12: 0.06–0.09 vs 0.22–0.32). Two weaknesses remain: the edits are larger in norm (10–18% when applied to all four heads with four phrasing directions), and in the trained phrasing L7.H0 and the L9 heads still don't return to the question (0.08 and 0.2), because there the fixed clause tokens also compete. I'll extend the design with a few clause-token directions (top principal directions of the trained clause's key offsets), restrict edits to heads that actually read the guess or the question, and evaluate layers 7 and 9 with 0, 2 or 4 clause directions.

```python
# Extend oblique design with clause-token directions (T phrasing) and head restriction; evaluate L7, L9 (and L10/L12 sanity)
def design2(l, fit_g, fit_n, r, clause_k=0):
    L=LP(l); th=THETA[l]; groups={}; Nv=[]; slots={}
    for s in fit_g:
        T_=targets(L['P'],Xof(s,l),s['p'],th)*L['gq']; cl=list(range(s['qs'][-1]+1,s['ue'])); oth=[t for t in range(0,s['p']+1) if t not in cl]; mo=T_[oth].mean(0)
        groups.setdefault(s['ph'],[]).append(T_[s['gs']].mean(0)-mo)
        if s['ph']=='T':
            for t in cl:
                if t in s['gs']: continue
                key=('pre',t-s['qs'][-1]) if t<s['gs'][0] else ('post',s['ue']-t)
                slots.setdefault(key,[]).append(T_[t]-mo)
    for s in fit_n:
        Tn=targets(L['P'],Xof(s,l),s['p'],th)*L['gq']; Nv.append(Tn-Tn.mean(0,keepdim=True))
    Dl=torch.stack([torch.stack(v).mean(0) for v in groups.values()])
    if clause_k>0:
        C=torch.stack([torch.stack(v).mean(0) for v in slots.values()]); Uc,Sc,Vc=torch.linalg.svd(C,full_matrices=False)
        Dl=torch.cat([Dl, Vc[:clause_k]*Sc[:clause_k,None]/np.sqrt(len(slots))])
    U,Sg,Vt=torch.linalg.svd(torch.cat(Nv),full_matrices=False)
    return Dl,Vt[:r]
