The logit lens on the original shows the same pattern in H and E. The guess is not linearly decodable at intermediate positions, and it becomes favoured at the decision position only in hidden state 12 (after layer 11): +3.3 in H, +2.8 in E. So the guess still arrives at the decision position around layers 11–12 in the guess-first phrasing, yet layer-11 attention to the guess token itself is small there (≤.09).

So I need to know what the decision position reads in H. I'll break decision-position attention into key categories (BOS, clause before the guess, the guess, the full stop after it, question tokens, question mark, turn markers, reply tokens) for each head in layers 9–13 and 17, original versus V3. If a specific category soaks up attention in H, for example the token right after the guess or the question tokens, that tells me which key direction a projector must target.

